// offset_tile: point loop offset by 1, clipped: I runs [1, 18) (18 = 1 + 2 x 8 + 1); row 0 of C is not written
//   oracle: untiled
// STRICT-LABEL: func.func @offset_tile
// STRICT: affine.for %{{[a-z0-9]+}} = 1 to 18 {
// STRICT-NEXT: affine.for %{{[a-z0-9]+}} = 0 to 19 {
// STRICT-NEXT: affine.for %{{[a-z0-9]+}} = 0 to 23 {
// STRICT-NEXT: affine.load
// STRICT-NOT: systolic.matmul_tile
// CHECK-LABEL: func.func @offset_tile
// CHECK: systolic.matmul_tile
// SREMARK: remark: affine multiply-accumulate nest: loop tiling as written untiled (docs/AFFINE_GEMM_MAPPING.md section 26.3): tile loop 0 (T = 8) dropped, point loop 1 runs [1, 18) (last tile 1 of 8); every point of the logical box is run by exactly one iteration (exact, Presburger); the order of the iterations is kept
// SREMARK: remark: affine GEMM not lowered to systolic.matmul_tile: floating-point reassociation is not permitted
